  "question": {
    "text": "The quadratic equations <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> have one root in common. The other roots of the first equation and the second equation are integers in the ratio <math><mn>4</mn><mi></mi><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Then the common root is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
